# Usage

Use when the user wants **serialized Sitecore items as YAML** under **`authoring/items/`** for **any** new or updated TSX component—then sync with XM Cloud / Sitecore CLI. **Do not** use Sitecore or Marketer MCP for this workflow.

Keep **`.sitecore/component-map.ts`** (or your app’s component map) aligned with the Json Rendering **`componentName`** value.

---

## 0) Fill the module table once per repo (then reuse)

Replace placeholders for **your** authoring layout. Example values are from this repo’s Bupa vertical only—swap for retail/teamviewer/etc.

| Placeholder | Meaning | Example (Bupa) |
|-------------|---------|----------------|
| `{{moduleKey}}` | Top-level folder under `authoring/items/` that holds serialized trees | `bupa` |
| `{{moduleDefinitionFile}}` | Module JSON next to `items/` (defines includes / roots) | `authoring/items/bupa-uk.module.json` |
| `{{sitecoreProjectKey}}` | Sitecore segment in `/templates/Project/…`, `/layout/Renderings/Project/…`, etc. | `bupa` |
| `{{siteKey}}` | Site folder name under `authoring/items/{{moduleKey}}/site/` | `bupa-uk` |
| `{{rootWebsitePath}}` | Site root item path in Sitecore | `/sitecore/content/bupa/bupa-uk` |
| `{{homeWebsitePath}}` | Home item path (link standard values) | `/sitecore/content/bupa/bupa-uk/home` |

**Derived paths (always derive from the table—do not hardcode another vertical’s names):**

- `{{serializationRoot}}` = `authoring/items/{{moduleKey}}/`
- **Templates:** `{{serializationRoot}}templatesProject/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/`
- **Json renderings:** `{{serializationRoot}}projectRenderings/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/`
- **Placeholder settings:** `{{serializationRoot}}projectPlaceholderSettings/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/`
- **Site content:** `{{serializationRoot}}site/{{siteKey}}/`

If your module JSON uses different include names, map them from **`{{moduleDefinitionFile}}`** instead of the rows above.

---

## 1) Name the new component (from TSX)

| Placeholder | Rule |
|-------------|------|
| `{{tsxFilePath}}` | Repo path to the component file, e.g. `industry-verticals/bupa/src/components/bupa/MyWidget.tsx` |
| `{{componentMapKey}}` | Exact string key in the Content SDK **component map** (often the TSX file base name) |
| `{{sitecoreBaseName}}` | Short name for **template folder**, **inner datasource template item**, **Json Rendering item name**, and **`{{sitecoreBaseName}} Folder`** template. Often = file base name, or strip a **known brand prefix** (e.g. `BupaMyWidget` → `MyWidget`)—**pick one rule per vertical and apply consistently**. |
| `{{dataFolderDisplayName}}` | Plural (or conventional) **site Data** subfolder for datasource instances | e.g. `MyWidgets` |
| `{{defaultDatasourceItemName}}` | First default item under that folder | e.g. `Default MyWidget` |

---

## 2) Pick a **reference component** to clone (not LinkBox-specific)

Choose **any** component in **`{{serializationRoot}}`** that already has the same **item shape** you need (datasource template + folder template + parameters + Json Rendering; optional placeholder settings).

| Placeholder | Meaning |
|-------------|---------|
| `{{referenceSitecoreBaseName}}` | That component’s short name (e.g. `LinkBoxCard`, `Title`, `Promo`—whatever exists in YAML) |
| `{{referenceSerializationPrefix}}` | Repo prefix to its files, e.g. `{{serializationRoot}}templatesProject/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/{{referenceSitecoreBaseName}}/` |

**Clone `Template:` / `Parent:` / `SharedFields` shapes** from the reference YAML; **generate new GUIDs** for every new item and fix all `Parent` / cross-references. Do **not** copy IDs from the reference into new items.

---

## Mandatory: YAML change log

For every create/update/delete:

### YAML change log

| Repo file | Action | What changed |
|-----------|--------|----------------|
| `{{serializationRoot}}…` | create / update / delete | Concrete hints: `componentName`, new field `Hint`, `Path:`, `__Masters`, deleted file, etc. |

Rules:

- **Create** — list each new file and main fields set.
- **Update** — each file + semantic before/after (e.g. “removed field YAML; TSX dropped prop”).
- **Delete** — path + reason.
- New IDs must be **unique** across the module.

---

## Template field rules (field definition YAML)

- **Image** — appropriate Sitecore type; **Source** `query:$siteMedia`; **Shared** when your vertical’s pattern requires it.
- **Rich Text** — Source `query:$xaRichTextProfile`.
- **General Link** — Source `query:$linkableHomes`; **Shared** when required.
- Other types — match existing patterns in **`{{referenceSerializationPrefix}}`**.

---

## Standard values

- Link fields: follow your vertical’s serialized link pattern (often home by ID).
- Image defaults: `<image mediaid="{GUID}" />` only when a media item exists in YAML.
- Keep datasource field items **1:1** with the TSX `fields` / `Fields` contract.

---

## Steps → YAML (generic patterns)

In all paths below, substitute **`{{serializationRoot}}`**, **`{{sitecoreProjectKey}}`**, **`{{sitecoreBaseName}}`**, **`{{siteKey}}`**.

### Step 1 — Template folder item

- **Create:** `{{serializationRoot}}templatesProject/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/{{sitecoreBaseName}}.yml`
- **Sitecore `Path:`:** `/sitecore/templates/Project/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/{{sitecoreBaseName}}`
- **Clone from:** `{{referenceSitecoreBaseName}}.yml` at the same templates level.

### Step 2 — Datasource template tree

Under `templatesProject/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/{{sitecoreBaseName}}/`:

- Inner template `{{sitecoreBaseName}}.yml`, section `Data.yml`, one yml per field, `__Standard Values.yml`
- **Clone** layout from `{{referenceSerializationPrefix}}` (adjust names, IDs, `Parent`).

### Step 3 — Datasource **folder** template

- `{{sitecoreBaseName}} Folder.yml` + `{{sitecoreBaseName}} Folder/__Standard Values.yml`
- Mirror **`{{referenceSitecoreBaseName}} Folder`** pattern (`__Masters`, icons).

### Step 4 — Rendering parameters template

- `{{sitecoreBaseName}} Parameters.yml`, child `Rendering Parameters.yml`, `__Standard Values.yml`
- Clone from reference **Parameters** tree (base templates: rendering params + dynamic placeholder + rendering id—same as your reference Json rendering component).

### Step 5 — Site Data insert options (if present in YAML)

If the repo serializes the item that controls **Insert Options** under `Data`, append the new **`{{sitecoreBaseName}} Folder`** template ID to `__Masters`. If not serialized, state **Step 5 N/A** in the change log.

### Step 6 — Site datasource folder + default item

- `{{serializationRoot}}site/{{siteKey}}/Data/{{dataFolderDisplayName}}.yml`
- `…/Data/{{dataFolderDisplayName}}/{{defaultDatasourceItemName}}.yml`
- **Paths** under `{{rootWebsitePath}}/Data/…`

### Step 7 — Json Rendering

- **Create:** `{{serializationRoot}}projectRenderings/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/{{sitecoreBaseName}}.yml`
- **`componentName`:** `{{componentMapKey}}`
- **Datasource / parameters / location:** same **shape** as reference rendering; replace names and GUIDs with the new template IDs/paths.

### Step 8 — Placeholder settings (only if TSX uses `<Placeholder />`)

- **Create:** `{{serializationRoot}}projectPlaceholderSettings/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/<kebab-slug>.yml`
- **Placeholder Key:** TSX pattern with dynamic segment replaced by `{*}` (e.g. `my-widgets-${id}` → `my-widgets-{*}`).
- **Allowed Controls:** Json Rendering IDs allowed in that placeholder.
- **Update** parent rendering(s): **`Placeholders`** shared field lists this placeholder settings item’s ID.

